eps about 61\\% of the gain over always-reliable, per-instance rank correlation is 0.58, and constants are hand-set and untuned. The results are limited to Kernel SHAP, three datasets and two budgets.\n123:Provenance of the constants matters for interpretation. The weights $0.5/0.2/0.3$, $0.6$, $0.02$, the fold count and the partition count are hand-set and were not tuned on instance labels. The values $0.84$ and $0.96$ are described in the configuration's notes as aggregate label means by budget from earlier search-plane evaluations (\\texttt{selected\\_config\\_NOTES.md}). The shrinkage weight is therefore a fixed constant, not an estimated empirical-Bayes weight; we use the term \\emph{empirical-Bayes-style} only for the structure of shrinking an unreliable per-unit estimate toward a prior derived from other data, as in Stein-type estimators \\citep{Efron1973Stein}.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
