{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgvr3vtnYrNDaFiikMvas","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MZJmnvt8ASjzPLV2KnTy6Z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b,cnt=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==cnt,(a,s.count(a))\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"On three held-out tabular datasets and three model families, mean agreement\",\n    \"On three tabular datasets that are disjoint by record hash from the search data (one is the complementary half of a German Credit split used in the search, so it is not an independent source dataset) and three model families, mean agreement\")\nrep(\"The permuted control keeps about 61\\\\% of the gain over always-reliable, per-instance rank correlation is 0.58, and constants are hand-set and untuned.\",\n    \"The permuted control keeps about 61\\\\% of the gain over always-reliable, per-instance rank correlation is 0.58, and the weights and shrinkage constants are hand-set and untuned, while the budget prior was taken from earlier search-plane aggregate label means.\")\nrep(\"on three tabular datasets and three model families that were held out from the selection of the diagnostic.\",\n    \"on three tabular datasets and three model families. The datasets are disjoint by record hash from the search data used to select the diagnostic; one of them (German Credit) is the complementary half of a search-plane split, so that result does not come from an independent source dataset.\")\nrep(\"The retained part is knowledge the diagnostic holds about the episode: chiefly the budget, through the prior, and any dataset- or family-level shifts in its simulated values.\",\n    \"The retained part is episode-level information that may include the budget (through the prior) and dataset- or family-level shifts in the simulated values; the evidence does not apportion it.\")\nrep(\"Most of the measured benefit is therefore consistent with knowing the budget and similar episode-level facts.\",\n    \"Most of the measured benefit is therefore episode-level rather than instance-specific; it may reflect the budget, dataset- or family-level calibration, or both, and the evidence does not apportion it.\")\nrep(\"\\\\caption{Constants of the frozen self-diagnostic. None was fitted to instance labels.}\",\n    \"\\\\caption{Constants of the frozen self-diagnostic. None was fitted to instance labels; the budget-prior values 0.84 and 0.96 are aggregate label means by budget taken from earlier search-plane evaluations.}\")\nrep(\"across three held-out datasets and three model families.\",\"across three datasets (disjoint by record hash from the search data) and three model families.\")\nrep(\"averaged over three held-out datasets, three model families\",\"averaged over three final datasets, three model families\")\nrep(\"Across the held-out datasets and model families,\",\"Across the final datasets and model families,\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"held-out\" paper.tex | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"main_comparison\\|composite\" analysis/build_figures.py | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1963,"cache_read_input_tokens":56646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1963},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0620ed1e-b8e9-439c-b133-0b78f4dcb175","uuid":"31903003-141a-402c-921b-c8007e9197b4","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:44:42.501Z","request_id":"req_011Cgvr3u97Bo9mco9fxmMQg"}
